<?php
/** User manual — HR manager edition: how the HR manager runs people, leave, training and evaluations in the portal.   GAS-CP-R63-003 */
return [
  'title' => 'Customer Portal — HR Manager Handbook',
  'lede'  => 'Everything the HR manager (and the Owner / administrators acting as HR) does in the portal: the people register and the employee card, the leave engine and balances, requests and approvals, leave periods and company closures, training and certificates, annual evaluations, off-boarding, the yearly cycle, the Community tools — with the routine of a day, a week and a year, and checklists.',
  'sections' => [
    ['id' => 'role', 'title' => 'Who is HR in the portal, and where things are', 'body' => [
      'Apps showing "Sync error" (v1.133.3): between 10 and 12 November 2026 the phone apps (Service Engineer, Golden PM, Golden HR and the customer app) could not reach the portal and showed "Sync error". This is repaired on the server — no app update is needed. Open the app and pull to refresh, or wait for the next automatic sync: reports, hours, photos and requests that were saved on the phone in the meantime are still in its queue and are sent now. If an app still shows the error, sign out and in again.',
      'Signed out when you come back (v1.127.7): the portal signs a person out when its last tab has been closed for more than about 45 seconds ("the browser was closed" — Settings › Login history › Sign out when the browser is closed; management can switch it off). Opening the portal after that leads straight to the sign-in page with that message — the dashboard no longer appears for a moment first. Going from the portal to the entry page goldensas.com and back in the same browser keeps you signed in while that page stays open.',
      'Three kinds of account do HR work. An account whose Golden A/S role is scoped "Planning only (HR)" sees the HR pages and nothing else of the portal (HR dashboard, Planning, HR requests, Leaves, Training, HR settings). An account with the "Owner" scope sees the whole portal plus every HR page and record, without administrator rights. Administrators have the same HR functions in addition to everything. Managers (the personal manager of an account or the manager of its discipline) are not HR: they only approve the requests, training applications and evaluations of their own people.',
      'The HR group in the left menu: 📊 HR dashboard — today\'s picture and the queues; 🏖 My leave — your own leave as an employee; 📝 HR requests — the approval queue (leave, training applications, evaluations of my people); 🏖 Leaves — who is away over a period, leave periods / groups and company closures; 🎓 Training — publish trainings, decide applications, record attendance and certificates; 🗂 HR — leave planning (Settings › HR) — People, Types, Rules, Balances, Imports, Reports. The Planning board (Work › Planning) is where every absence finally lands, next to the project work.',
      'What you can see that others cannot: the personal and payroll data of the employee card, the documents of the card, the private HR ↔ employee messages, the balances of everybody, the audit trail of every change. Identification and bank numbers appear masked in the change log; the employee sees his own data and documents on My leave and nothing of anybody else.',
      ['ul' => ['A new employee: create the card (People › + Person) or import the register; link or create the portal account (➕ Account on the People tab pre-fills a staff account from the card); record the Hiring event with the contract; check the balances of the year; start the onboarding checklist (Community › Onboarding) and name a buddy; publish the introductory training.', 'Somebody leaves: record the Termination event on the card (closes the employment period, marks the person as left, deactivates the staff account) and run the release-of-contract checklist that appears below it.', 'Every day: HR dashboard — requests waiting, contracts expiring, unread messages, certificates expiring, who is away.', 'Every year on 1 January: the checklist in the yearly cycle section.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'dashboard', 'title' => 'HR dashboard — the daily round', 'body' => [
      'The HR dashboard (first page of HR-only accounts; Owner / administrators: HR › HR dashboard) answers the daily questions in one screen: who is away today and this week (the board chips per day), the requests waiting for your decision, contracts expiring within 90 days (red when past), unread employee messages, certificates expiring within 90 days, the celebrations of the next 30 days (birthdays with the age, name days), headcount and the annual-leave totals of the year, and the table of every employee with entitled / carried over / taken / pending / available — green, gold at 3 days or fewer, red when negative — sorted so the people with the least leave left come first. Every name opens the employee card.',
      ['ol' => ['Open the dashboard; decide the pending requests (HR requests) — leave first, then training applications.', 'Look at the contracts expiring: 60 days before a fixed-term end the People tab warns; decide renewal (Contract change event) or termination.', 'Answer the unread employee messages (the thread is on the card › Messages with HR).', 'Check the red / gold balances: a negative balance usually means a record counted twice (see Balances).', 'Glance at the celebrations and send the company wishes where the day has come.']],
      ['fig' => 'g-dashboard.jpg', 'cap' => 'The dashboard — the HR version replaces the project blocks with the HR queues'],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'people', 'title' => 'People register and the employee card', 'body' => [
      'People (HR › HR settings › People): every Golden A/S employee, with or without a portal account. The filter row above the list searches by Latin or Greek name, employee code, e-mail or job title and filters by discipline, employed / left / everyone, technical or not, employment kind, country, contract type, with or without account; the counter shows matches / total. ➕ Account next to a person without an account opens the account form pre-filled from the card and links the two on save. 📜 opens the full leave history of the person; 🪪 opens the card.',
      'The employee card is one record per person that stays for life. Tabs: 🪪 Data — identity, department, job title, contract, hiring date, prior service, marital status, working days, children (number and birth years — they drive maternity / paternity and the child allowance), jurisdiction (GR / IT rule set), employment kind (employee / contractor), and Personal data (HR only: personal e-mail, phones, home address, date of birth, AMKA, ΑΦΜ, ΔΟΥ, ID, passport, IBAN, bank, emergency contact, father\'s / mother\'s / spouse name, nationality, birth place, blood group, education, grade, transport, work phone and extension, postcode / city / country, gross salary, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, payroll code). 📑 Employment periods — Hiring, Contract change, Termination, Re-hiring events with documents; the off-boarding checklist appears under a termination. ✅ HR requests — the requests of this person, with approve / reject in place. 💬 Messages with HR — the private thread. 📎 Documents — everything filed on the card (contracts, certificates, training certificates, evaluations). 🗓 Entitlements — the balance engine per year and type, with lock / unlock and the carry-over. 🏷 Leave types — types switched off for this person. 🎓 Training — the training record and certificates. 📈 Evaluations — the annual evaluations and the evolution chart. 🕘 Changes — the audit trail (who changed what, when; secrets masked).',
      'Service: the portal computes the service at Golden A/S from the employment periods, adds the prior service at other employers (years + months on the card) and shows the total; the leave engine uses the total for the seniority steps. Keep the prior service as the accountant\'s register states it.',
      ['ul' => ['Documents: PDF, images, Word, 15 MB each, stored outside the web root; only HR / administrators and the person himself can open them. Kinds: contract, hiring form, termination notice, ΕΡΓΑΝΗ form, identity / permit, certificate, training, evaluation, other.', 'Deleting: the last employment event can be deleted while it has no documents; a card is never deleted — mark the person as left.', 'Portal account and card: one account ↔ one card. The approver of the person is the personal manager of the account, else the manager of the discipline (Settings › Portal accounts / Disciplines); the department head is the fallback for people without an account.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'imports', 'title' => 'Imports — register, personal data, prior service, balances, past leave', 'body' => [
      'Departments are the portal disciplines (Settings › Disciplines, administrators) — one list for accounts, Planning and HR; if an import ever produced a duplicate, an administrator merges it there (Merge into…), nothing is lost. The import matches department names loosely and creates a new discipline only when you tick "create unknown departments" on the preview. The pre-filled template (People › Excel template) exports every field of every card exactly as stored — the personal / payroll columns only when you are signed in as HR or Owner (a plain administrator gets the 22 general columns). The import preview warns when a file carries personal columns the signed-in account cannot write. All imports are on HR › HR settings › People / Import and take Excel files with a header row; the portal shows a preview and applies only when you confirm. Existing people are recognised by Greek name, Latin name or e-mail and updated; empty cells never erase data; unknown departments are created and flagged.',
      ['ol' => ['People register (Import people from Excel): download the template first — it is pre-filled with the current people and carries every card column, personal and payroll data included (father\'s / mother\'s / spouse name, nationality, passport, blood group, education, grade, transport, phones, address, AMKA, ΑΦΜ, ΔΟΥ, ID, IBAN, bank, gross salary, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, payroll code). An invalid value (a 10-digit AMKA, a wrong IBAN check digit) is skipped with a warning and the rest of the row is saved. The Latin name must be exactly the name on the card, otherwise a second card is created — fix the spelling in the sheet before applying.', 'Prior service: the same import; columns Prior service (years) and (months) as the accountant\'s register states them.', 'Balances (Import balances): the accountant\'s balances per person and type for a year, with "Balances as of <date>" — the cut-over date. From that date the engine counts only the records after it; everything before is in the imported opening balance, so nothing is counted twice. Use it once at go-live and whenever you re-align with the accountant.', 'Past leave records (Import leave records): Email / names, Type code, From, To, Days, Hours, Status, Reason — for history; rows already in the portal are skipped. Records before the cut-over date are "history only" and do not touch the balance.', 'Staff list of the planning board (Import Excel matrix on Planning): absences per day for a month — used by the PMs; not an HR import.']],
      'Watch for: a negative available balance after an import almost always means the opening balance already contained days that are also present as 2026 records — set the cut-over date to the date of the accountant\'s balance and re-import.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'types_rules', 'title' => 'Leave types, rules and the balance engine', 'body' => [
      'Leave types (HR settings › Types): code, name in five languages, kind on the board, counts against the entitlement, reason required, unit (days or hours), HR only (no manager stage — sick, parental, strike, paternity …), document required, paid, consumes annual leave (hour types: 8 hours = 1 day), maximum per year (statutory caps: PAT 14, MAR 5, CAR 5, FMJ 2, SCH 32 h …), once per birth (maternity / paternity), transferable or not. Built-in types are renamed only; delete only unused ones. A type can be switched off for one person on the card › Leave types.',
      'Rules (HR settings › Leave rules, validated with the accountant): annual leave is computed automatically — in the calendar year of hiring the full-year days pro rata to the days worked; 21 days in the second calendar year, 22 from the third; 25 after 10 years at Golden A/S or 12 years of total service; 26 after 25 years; 5-day and 6-day week variants; the Italian rule set for the branch; contractors have no statutory allowance. The card › Entitlements shows per type the statutory basis, the computed days, the mode (🔒 automatic / 🔓 fixed by HR), taken, pending and available. Unlock to type a different figure; lock to return to the engine. Carry-over: the unused days of the previous year are carried according to the rule (transferable types only) — the Entitlements tab has the carry / transfer action per person.',
      'Maternity / paternity: once per birth; the children\'s birth years on the card tell the engine which birth a request belongs to; days already taken at another employer for the same birth are deducted ("taken elsewhere" on the request). Other types are not transferable between employers.',
      ['ul' => ['Early leaves / late arrivals (EARLY) and any other hour type marked "consumes annual leave" are a company permission, not a statutory leave (Greek law grants annual leave in working days only): the hours accumulate and only each completed 8 hours takes one day of annual leave — the remainder is shown under the annual balance on My leave ("4 h accumulated · 4 h to the next day") and waits for the next hours; at year end decide with the accountant whether a remainder is waived or charged. Write the rule in the work regulation.', 'Days are always working days: weekends and the public holidays of the person\'s work calendar are never charged (Settings › Work calendars; a year nobody generated falls back to the country\'s public holidays, Orthodox Easter included).', 'Hour types (EARLY, SCH …) accumulate in hours; every 8 hours consume one day of annual leave where the type says so.', 'Balances per person and year are visible to the person on My leave and to the managers for their people.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'requests', 'title' => 'Requests and approvals', 'body' => [
      'The employee requests leave on My leave (type, dates or hours, reason, document when the type requires it); the manager approves or rejects (HR-only types skip this stage); HR approves or rejects; on approval the portal writes the days to the Planning board (one entry per working day with the type and reason) and the balance moves from pending to taken. Each step notifies the next person and the employee. HR can also enter a request on behalf of an employee (HR requests › New request for …) — for sick leave with the certificate, for leave agreed verbally — and can cancel or correct a record from the card › HR requests.',
      ['ol' => ['HR requests page: the queue shows the requests at your stage first (pending HR), then the manager stage, with the balance of the person next to each request; filter by year and status; per-person history from 📜.', 'Decide with a note — the note goes to the employee. A rejection returns the days to the balance; a cancellation by the employee is possible while the request is pending.', 'Documents attached (medical certificates …) are visible to the employee, the approver and HR only.', 'The same page carries the Training applications queue and the Evaluations of my people (for managers — HR sees everyone).']],
      ['fig' => 'flow-timesheet.svg', 'cap' => 'The approval ladder — requested by the employee, manager, HR, then the board'],
      'Managers may also take the manager-stage decision from the Golden PM app on their phone, after entering their authenticator code; the portal records it as a normal decision with the suffix "(mobile app)" and notifies HR as usual. The HR stage, decisions on behalf of an absent manager and HR-only types are decided in the portal only.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'leaves', 'title' => 'Leaves page — who is away, leave periods, company closures', 'body' => [
      'HR › Leaves: who is away over any period (up to three months) for the whole company or one discipline — a day matrix with the leave-type code per person and day (gold = pending), totals per type and person-days; the previous / next month buttons move the window; the assistant box answers questions about the matrix.',
      'Leave periods / groups: HR creates a period (name, type, dates, target: whole company / disciplines / people, maximum people, note, status). Open periods appear on My leave of the people targeted; they join with their own dates inside the period; the manager approves; the request is then approved automatically and lands on the board. Assign to all creates an approved record for everybody targeted at once (people with an overlapping request are skipped and listed); Undo removes what Assign to all created (never what people joined themselves); 🔄 Recount days recomputes the days of an applied period without weekends and holidays and rewrites the board.',
      'Company closure: tick "Company closure" on a period for leave the company imposes (Christmas week, August). Staff see it as 🔒 Mandatory on My leave with "assigned by HR" and cannot join or opt out; you assign it with Assign to all. The days are charged to the annual leave as working days only.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'training', 'title' => 'Training and certificates', 'body' => [
      'HR › Training: publish a training — kind introductory (new hires), internal (given by Golden A/S) or external (provider, trainer, location) — with dates, hours, places, apply-by date, cost, whether a certificate is issued, who is invited (whole company, disciplines or chosen people) and the programme. Saving an open training notifies the people invited; they apply from My leave › Training opportunities; applications reach you and the person\'s manager (HR requests › Training applications) — approve or reject, the employee is notified. You can also add people directly (approved).',
      ['ol' => ['After the training: open it, set each participant to attended / absent, type the result (Pass · 85 %), and for trainings with a certificate the number, issue date, valid-until date and upload the scanned copy — it is filed on the card › Documents as kind "training".', 'Certificates expiring within 90 days show on the HR dashboard and on the Training page: plan the refresher training before they expire.', 'The employee card › 🎓 Training shows the record with the participation summary (trainings attended, hours, certificates, evaluations); the employee sees the same on My leave › My trainings.', 'Close the training (status Completed) when everything is recorded; Cancelled keeps the record but hides it from the opportunities.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'evaluations', 'title' => 'Annual evaluations', 'body' => [
      'One evaluation per employee and year, written by HR (card › 📈 Evaluations) or by the manager (HR requests › Evaluations of my people › the person): eight criteria scored 1–5 — quality of work, productivity, technical skills, teamwork, initiative, reliability, safety & procedures, communication — the overall score is the average; strengths, areas to improve, goals for next year, training needs, comments. Draft is visible to HR and the manager only. Final notifies the employee, who reads it on My leave › My evaluations, may add a comment and acknowledges it (status Acknowledged, logged in the card changes). Once final only HR can change it.',
      'Two criteria are computed by the portal and included in the overall score: Training participation (trainings attended and hours in the year, ranked among active colleagues — top 20 % = 5, next 20 % = 4, next 30 % = 3, rest = 2, none = 1) and Attendance & consistency (starts at 5; −1 per 16 h of early leaves / late arrivals, −1 per 3 days of unplanned absence — unpaid or other absence; sick leave is shown but not penalised —, −1 per 3 leave requests asked less than 2 days ahead). The form shows them read-only with the figures behind them, and the targets of the year with their achievement. Every employee sees the same rules and his computed scores so far on My leave › How we evaluate you.',
      'The Evolution chart on the tab shows the overall score per year with the participation line (trainings attended, hours, certificates) — use it in the yearly review meeting and to feed the training programme (the training-needs text of every final evaluation is your list for next year).',
      ['ul' => ['Recommended calendar: managers write drafts in November, HR reviews in December, finals and employee acknowledgements by 31 January.', 'Keep the scoring scale consistent across managers: 3 = meets expectations; reserve 5 for outstanding, documented cases.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'targets', 'title' => 'Targets for departments and individuals', 'body' => [
      'HR › Targets: the targets of the year for the company, each department and each person — title, how it is measured, the target value and unit, due date, weight 1–5 (importance in the evaluation), progress % and status (open, on track, at risk, achieved, missed, cancelled), description and closing remarks. You manage all of them; a manager manages those of his disciplines and his people. Creating a target notifies the people concerned; everybody sees the targets that concern him on My leave › My targets and updates the progress of his own — achieved / missed are set by the manager or by you at year end. Every update is logged (History under the target). The evaluation panel of a person sums his targets (achieved, average progress).',
      'Assistant: ✨ Propose on the Targets page drafts 4–6 SMART targets for a department or a person from the facts in the portal — people and roles, last year\'s targets and results, trainings, computed scores, the last evaluation — plus your brief; Add each with one click or Edit it first. On the evaluation panel ✨ Draft the evaluation proposes scores and texts from the year\'s facts for you to review; Ask answers questions about the person\'s year. Both need the pages Evaluations and Targets enabled under Settings › Assistant › Pages; personal and payroll data are never sent.',
      ['ol' => ['January: set the company targets (HR / management) and ask every manager to enter the department and individual targets of his people by end of January — SMART: measurable, with a due date.', 'Quarterly: filter the year, sort out the at-risk ones, remind the managers to update the progress.', 'November: close the targets (achieved / missed with the closing remark) before the evaluations are written.', 'The "How we evaluate you" note at the bottom of the page is what every employee reads on My leave — write there what the company expects this year, how the prize and the ranking work.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'assistant', 'title' => 'HR Assistant — guided flows approved by HR (R67-001)', 'body' => [
      'HR › HR Assistant is a guided, step-by-step way to collect data without e-mails and Excel sheets: the person fills the flow, the portal validates every value at entry, and nothing reaches the employee card before HR approves. The first flow is "My card": every employee with a card linked to his account completes or corrects his own personal data. The hiring, leaving and dismissal flows follow on the same engine (R67-002 / R67-003).',
      ['ul' => [
        'What the employee can propose: names, date and place of birth, nationality, gender, marital status, children; personal e-mail, phones, address, emergency contact; AMKA, ΑΦΜ and tax office, ID / passport, IBAN and bank, blood group; education, transport, work phone. What stays with HR only: gross salary, payroll code, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, grade, hiring date, prior service, contract, department.',
        'Validation at entry: AMKA 11 digits whose first six form a date — when that date differs from the date of birth (certificate issued later) the employee ticks "My AMKA was issued with this date" and the field carries a note for you to check; ΑΦΜ with its check digit, IBAN check digits, plausible dates, children\'s years as four-digit years. A wrong value cannot be submitted.',
        'Assistant: on each step the employee can write his details in his own words or photograph his ID card / passport; the assistant proposes values for that step only, the employee presses Use per value, and the photo is not stored (the scan goes to the Documents step). The page "HR Assistant" must be enabled in Settings › Assistant › Pages for the staff who should have it.',
        'Security: the identification numbers of an open flow are stored encrypted (libsodium, key derived from the instance and a random salt in cp_settings) and decrypted for the owner and HR only; the identification step and the submission ask for the authenticator code when the account has 2FA; the GDPR notice (controller, purpose, legal basis, recipients, retention, rights) is accepted on the first step and the acceptance is logged with time and address.',
        'To review: HR › HR Assistant lists the submitted flows (badge on the menu, list on the HR dashboard). Open one: every proposed value is shown next to the card value with its source (employee / assistant / document). Per field: ✔ approve or ✖ reject with a note. For the flow: "Approve & apply" writes every field not rejected to the card through the normal card save (the change log on the card shows "HR Assistant HRA-…"), files the documents under the card\'s Documents tab and notifies the employee; "Return for corrections" sends it back as a draft with your note; "Reject" closes it.',
        'Housekeeping: a draft idle for 7 days and a submission waiting for 3 days are reminded once a day; the staged values and files of applied, rejected or withdrawn flows are deleted 90 days after the decision — the flow row and its log stay.',
        'Flow templates (HR › HR Assistant › Flow templates): steps, fields per step, required fields, documents per step and approvers per flow kind and per branch (* or GR / GIT), as JSON. Only the fixed catalogue of employee fields is accepted; the built-in default is used when no active template exists.',
      ]],
      ['tip' => 'Ask the staff to complete their cards before the payroll import: HR › People shows who has no personal data, and every employee sees the completeness of his card on My leave with the button to start.'],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'recruiting', 'title' => 'Recruiting — careers website, screening, evaluation (v1.106.0 – v1.110.2)', 'body' => [
      'E-mail card — draft in your Outlook (v1.131.1): the button "Draft in my Outlook" places the message in the Drafts folder of your own Microsoft 365 mailbox — in HTML format, with the recipients, Cc, subject, text and the ticked attachments (up to 25 MB). Open Outlook › Drafts — the new Outlook, Outlook on the web and the phone all show it within a few seconds — change what you like and press Send; it is sent from your address like any message you write yourself. The portal also shows a button that opens the draft in Outlook on the web. Use it when you want to read or edit the message before it leaves; use "Send now" when it can go as it is. The file "Draft file for classic Outlook (.eml)" stays for the classic Outlook only. Administrators: this button needs the application permission Mail.ReadWrite (with admin consent) on the portal mailer in Microsoft Entra; without it the portal answers that Microsoft 365 did not allow the draft.',
      'E-mail card — send from your own mailbox (v1.131.0): besides the Outlook draft, the card has the button "Send now from my mailbox" — the message leaves at once through Microsoft 365 from your own address, in HTML format with the ticked attachments, and is kept in the Sent Items of your Outlook; replies come to you. The portal asks for confirmation first. Limits: attachments up to 2,9 MB together, 30 recipients, 40 messages per hour. The Outlook draft (.eml) now opens in HTML format in classic Outlook.',
      'E-mail to a candidate (v1.110.0): the ✉ E-mail button on the application opens the portal e-mail card — the candidate is already in To, the template is pre-selected from the status (message, shortlisted, interview invitation, offer, not selected; texts in the candidate\'s language, editable under Settings › E-mail templates), and you get an Outlook draft (.eml) or your mail app with everything filled in. Each prepared e-mail is written to the application log. The checkbox "E-mail the candidate about this status" in the Decision box is the other path — the portal sends that one itself when you save a status.',
      'Notifications (v1.110.0): HR items — leave requests, HR messages, trainings, evaluations, HR assistant, recruiting — appear under the HR tab of the bell and the Notifications page, no longer under Work.',
      'Screening sets (v1.109.2 – v1.109.3): twelve sets come ready — ENG-STD-7 for engineers and technicians (7 questions, pass 6), PM-STD-8 for project managers, and one per role: IT-STD-8 (IT engineers), MEC-STD-8 (mechanical), AUT-STD-8 (automation), SRV-STD-8 (service engineers), ACC-STD-8 (accounting), UX-STD-8 (UI/UX designers), PRD-STD-8 (product designers), SAL-STD-8 (sales engineers), PRC-STD-8 (procurement), SAS-STD-8 (sales assistants) — each six situational questions for the role plus the two loyalty questions, pass 7 of 8; the loyalty group is a knock-out in all of them. Pick the set on the vacancy; edit questions or add sets under Recruiting › Screening sets — the website renders whatever the vacancy names.',
      'Website refresh (v1.110.2): the careers page shows a change to a vacancy or event within seconds of Save — the portal tells the website to drop its cache (the website keeps a 2-minute copy only as a fallback; a browser may hold its own copy for 30 s, so refresh the page). Event times are published with the Athens time zone.',
      'Vacancy and event codes (v1.109.1, v1.110.1): every vacancy gets a code VAC-year-number and every selection event EVT-year-number automatically; the form shows the next code in a read-only field before the first save and the fixed code afterwards — you only type the title.',
      'Assistant draft (v1.109.0): on the vacancy form, describe the role in a few words in the "Assistant — draft the vacancy" box and press Draft. The assistant fills title, summary, description, requirements, tags, location, type, seniority and — when the brief implies them — discipline and branch, keeping what you had already typed. The draft sits in the form until you press Save (or Discard); only the form fields are sent to the assistant, never candidate data. The administrator enables the page under Settings › Assistant (page "Recruiting") and the usual monthly cap applies.',
      'Departments on vacancies are the portal Disciplines (Settings › Disciplines) — the same structure the HR registry uses since v1.62.0; there is no separate HR department list (v1.108.3).',
      'HR › Recruiting is the system of record behind goldenas.com.gr/careers. The website stores no HR data: it renders what you publish here and posts everything candidates submit back to the portal through its own server-side proxy (the browser never reaches the portal and never sees the site key).',
      ['ul' => [
        'Vacancies: title, department, branch, location, type, seniority, summary, description, requirements (one per line), tags, hiring manager, screening set, closing date; Draft → Open → Closed / Filled. "Publish on goldenas.com.gr/careers" puts an open vacancy on the website within five minutes (the site caches reads). The hiring manager may read the vacancy, its applications and CVs without being HR.',
        'Online selection events (selection day, webinar, Q&A): date and duration, platform and join link (sent to registrants by e-mail, never shown on the website), capacity, registration deadline, the vacancies they serve. The registration list shows attendance and result per registrant; the website shows the seats left and refuses duplicates (409) and full or closed events (410).',
        'Screening sets: the mindset questionnaire the website renders (questions, groups, options). Option scores and the knock-out groups (e.g. loyalty) stay in the portal — the browser only receives texts. The portal scores every submission itself: pass threshold reached and every knock-out question scored → the candidate may upload a CV (one-time token, PDF / Word ≤ 8 MB, stored outside the web root); otherwise the application is recorded as failed and the candidate is invited to the online events.',
        'Applications: one per e-mail and vacancy (duplicates are refused). The card shows the candidate, screening score and answers, the CV (download for HR and the hiring manager only), event registrations, the pipeline status (screened › CV received › shortlisted › interview › offer › hired / rejected / withdrawn), rating, owner and HR notes. Shortlisted / offer / rejected can e-mail the candidate with one tick (needs the candidate From address in ⚙). Hired creates the person card in HR › People.',
        'Evaluation (R91-001): every interviewer adds a scorecard per stage (CV review, phone, technical, practical / case, final) — six weighted criteria scored 1–5 (technical knowledge 25 %, marine / shipyard experience 20 %, problem solving 15 %, learning attitude 15 %, loyalty & long-term commitment 15 %, teamwork 10 %; weights editable in ⚙) giving a 0–100 total plus a recommendation (strong hire / hire / hold / no hire). The card shows per-criterion averages and how the interviewers lean; the vacancy ranks its candidates by evaluation average, then screening score.',
        'Interviews: planned per stage (online / on site / phone, link or location, interviewers, duration); planning moves the candidate to Interview and can e-mail the invitation; done / no-show / cancelled are tracked.',
        'Talent pool: spontaneous requests from the website ("register your interest"), with area and message.',
        '⚙ Recruiting settings: allowed website origin, the site key (create / rotate — it is shown in full once, right after creation; copy it then into the website repository secret PORTAL_RC_KEY), retention months (default 6), CV size limit, HR mailbox for notifications, candidate From address (empty = no e-mails to candidates, messages stay in the log), evaluation criteria and weights.',
        'Data retention (GDPR): once a day the portal deletes unsuccessful applications (with their CV), event registrations and talent-pool entries older than the retention period, keeps candidates in an active pipeline (shortlisted / interview / offer) and anonymises hired ones; every run logs counts only. "Run retention now" runs it immediately.',
        'Security: the website endpoint (customer/rcr_feed.php) answers public reads only for the allowed origin and accepts writes only with the site key (constant-time comparison), rate-limited per visitor IP and per e-mail; it never returns option scores, join links, HR notes or anything about other candidates; keys are never shown after the first display.',
      ]],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'offboarding', 'title' => 'Off-boarding — release of a contract', 'body' => [
      'Record the Termination event on the card › Employment periods (reason: resignation, dismissal, end of contract, retirement, mutual, other; date; documents). The portal closes the employment period, marks the person as left, deactivates a staff portal account and shows the release-of-contract checklist under the event — the Greek list (ΕΡΓΑΝΗ notice, final pay and leave compensation, insurance, equipment and keys, access revocation, exit interview …) or the Italian one for the branch. Tick the items as they are done; the HR dashboard lists the pending off-boardings until the checklist is complete. The card, its documents and its history stay; a Re-hiring event re-opens a period on the same card.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'year', 'title' => 'The yearly cycle — 1 January checklist', 'body' => [
      ['ol' => ['Generate the public holidays of the new year for every work calendar (Settings › Work calendars › Generate) — the engine falls back to the standard list, but generating lets you add the local ones.', 'Check the leave rules against the accountant\'s circular (statutory changes) — HR settings › Leave rules.', 'Open the Entitlements of the new year: the engine computes every annual allowance; review the people with a seniority step this year (10 / 12 / 25 years) and the part-timers.', 'Carry-over: run the carry / transfer for the transferable types; confirm the figures with the accountant and lock.', 'Children born last year: enter the birth years on the cards (maternity / paternity).', 'Create the company closures of the year (Leaves › periods, Company closure) and the summer leave groups; assign the closures.', 'Publish the training plan of the year from the training-needs of the evaluations; schedule the refresher trainings for certificates expiring.', 'Export the HR report of the closed year (Planning › HR report › Excel) and file it with the accountant\'s balances.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'community', 'title' => 'Community tools HR owns', 'body' => [
      'Community (🤝): wishes on birthdays, name days, work anniversaries and new colleagues (the dashboard card, 14 days ahead); kudos between colleagues; the noticeboard with posts, polls and photos — HR publishes the company news and can pin a post; badges earned from the work in the portal; winner of the month — HR or the management names the winner of the previous month and the prize (Ranking › Name the winner; default prize text in Settings, key soc_prize); onboarding — HR starts the checklist of a new colleague and names a buddy; the morning nudge and the Monday digest are posted by the portal itself.',
      ['ul' => ['Company card on a celebration: write the wish from the HR account on the day — it is shown on the person\'s wishes wall with the others.', 'Keep the noticeboard alive: one post a week (a vessel delivered, a FAT passed, a newborn) keeps people coming back.', 'The winner of the month is announced to everybody — name it in the first days of the month.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'mobile_hr', 'title' => 'Golden HR — the HR app for iPhone (v1.82.0)', 'body' => [
      'Golden HR (customer/mobile-hr/, App Store bundle gr.goldenas.hr, iPhone only) is the fourth client of the portal, for the HR role, the Owner and the CEO — nobody else can sign in, whatever else they manage, and the check runs on every request. It is the mirror of Golden PM: the same sign-in (e-mail + password + authenticator code, or a passkey added under More), the same self-update, but a stricter lock — Face ID / Touch ID is asked on every cold start and after 15 minutes in the background or without a touch; there is no switch to turn that off, and a phone without Face ID / Touch ID cannot use the app.',
      ['ul' => ['Inbox: the leave / absence requests waiting for HR (and those still at the manager stage, which HR may decide as on the web), training applications and the timesheets you personally approve. Approve / Reject with a note (mandatory to reject) and, when your account has an authenticator, its 6-digit code — the decision goes through the portal\'s own hr_request_decide / ts_decide with the audit line "(Golden HR app)". Offline decisions wait in the outbox and are sent when the phone is online; a request decided meanwhile in the portal comes back as "no longer pending". Decided: the year\'s history.',
                'People: the directory of active staff — name, title, department / discipline, branch, work e-mail and phones, manager, hire date, contract type and end, with who is away today; search by name / title / department; the "Expiring soon" card lists contract ends within 60 days and certificates within 90 days. The person page adds this year\'s leave balances, the next absences and the HR message thread. Not in the app, by design: salary and payroll, bank, AMKA / AFM, identity documents, address and family, evaluations, targets, documents.',
                'Messages: the HR message threads with employees (the same threads as the employee card › Messages and the employees\' My HR in Golden PM / Service); unread badge on the tab; a reply notifies the employee as from the web.',
                'Calendar: the next four weeks day by day — who is away (leave code, pending in amber) and the public holidays of each work calendar; Leave balances: every person\'s balances of the year, searchable.',
                'More: account, language, Lock app, Sign out, passkeys, the outbox; the Mobile apps card of Settings › Login history shows the minimum app version per app (Golden HR included) and the registered devices.']],
      'Building and publishing: GitHub › Actions › Build iOS app › app "hr" (provisioning profile variable IOS_PROFILE_HR, App ID gr.goldenas.hr with Push + Associated Domains, an App Store Connect record "Golden HR"); apple-app-site-association must list TEAMID.gr.goldenas.hr for passkeys. The Android workflow has no "hr" option on purpose.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'privacy', 'title' => 'Data protection and audit', 'body' => [
      'Personal and payroll data are visible to HR and Owner accounts only (plain administrators do not see them, nor the age on the celebrations, nor the personal columns of an import); the employee sees his own. Identification and bank numbers are masked in the change log and in the previews. Documents live outside the web root and are streamed only to the people entitled. Every change on a card is logged (card › Changes) with the user and the time. Keep the import files in the HR folder, not on shared drives; the portal never e-mails personal data. Access is removed by deactivating the account (Settings › Portal accounts) or by the Termination event.',
        'Upload limits (v1.84.2): the server accepts up to 60 files per upload, 15 MB per file (20 MB elsewhere in the portal) and 256 MB per request — the hint under every file field shows the live figures. Choose more than that and the field turns red and the button is disabled before anything is sent; if a batch still exceeds the server limit you get a clear message instead of the old "session expired" bounce, and if the server trimmed a batch you are told how many were received. Beyond the limits: upload in batches.',
      'Personnel file (v1.85.1): the documents on a person\'s card (Documents tab, documents filed with an employment event) are visible, uploadable and deletable by the HR role and the Owner / CEO scope only — administrators do not see the tab, the file links or the file field, and a direct link to a document answers 403; the person sees his own documents. HR also has Support in its menu — the portal-requests card to report a problem or ask for a change — without the customers\' ticket inbox.',
      'HR management for HR, Owner and CEO only (v1.86.4): administrators no longer open the HR dashboard, the people cards, the HR settings or the HR tab of Settings — an administrator sees only his own data (My leave, requests, account) like every employee, unless his Golden A/S role is HR, Owner or CEO (the role named "CEO" counts as Owner for HR, including personal data and the personnel file). The HR dashboard has a search box (name, code, e-mail, title, department) and an Employed / Left / All switch above the balances table; people who left are greyed with a "Left" pill; the 👥 People button opens the full people list with its filters.',
      'Leaves allowed by law (v1.86.5): My leave, the Service app\'s My HR and the HR app no longer list parental, paternity / maternity, marriage, carer, force majeure, child illness, study, school hours, sick and L.104 leave among the entitlements. They sit in their own block "Allowed by law — on request" with the ceiling the law provides ("up to 5", "per event") and what was taken — never an "available" figure — with a note that they are not an entitlement to be used up but what the law allows when the event occurs, on request and with the supporting document. Annual leave, paid hours and early-leave hours remain entitlements.',
      'Reason and medical certificate (v1.87.0): every leave request needs a reason chosen from a list that follows the leave type (vacation, personal, family, bereavement, wedding, exams, public duty, force majeure … for leave; illness, accident, medical examination, surgery, hospitalisation for sick; birth, child care, child illness, school, prenatal for parental); "Other" needs a description. The manager may correct the reason when approving (the decision row has the reason selector) and HR may correct it at any time (✎ Correct reason under the request). A request for a medical reason may be sent without the doctor\'s certificate: it gets a due date 5 working days after the first day of absence, shown as a gold "certificate due by" pill (red when overdue) with an Upload button — on My leave, in the Service app and for HR under the request. The employee is reminded the day before, employee and HR when it is overdue; the HR dashboard lists the certificates still due. Works the same in the Service app (0.6.15) and the Golden HR app (1.0.3).',
      'Balance breakdown (v1.87.5): on a person\'s Entitlements tab every annual-leave year row has a Σ button that unfolds every figure behind the available days — entitled, carry-over, opening, each request with its days (approved subtracts, pending in brackets), board days typed without a request, annual-consuming hour types — and ends with the formula. Greyed lines are not counted and say why: starts in another year (counted there), history only (flagged not counted at import), or before the cut-over date (already inside the opening figure). When a balance looks wrong, this is where to look first.',
      'Opening taken days (v1.87.6): the Edit form of a year on the Entitlements tab now has an "Opening" field next to the entitled days — the days already taken before the portal counted the year (paper records, cut-over). Change it with a reason; the change is logged in the person\'s audit. The same figure is also in Settings › HR › Entitlements, column Opening.',
      'Pending requests across years (v1.88.0): the "Pending requests" tile and the Open filter of the HR requests page list the open requests of every year — a request for next January no longer disappears behind the year filter, which left the page showing only the "New request for…" form.',
      'Missing supporting documents (v1.87.1): My leave opens with a notice listing the requests that still lack their document — a medical certificate with its due date (red when overdue) or a type that requires a document filed without one — each with its upload button below; the Service app shows the same notice on My HR and a red badge on the home card; on the HR side the person\'s card carries a "📄 n supporting document(s) missing" pill on the Requests tab and the HR dashboard lists the medical certificates due. Leave reasons are translated in all portal languages (EN, EL, IT, BG, UK) on the web and in the apps.',
    ]],
  ],
];
